# A vendored snapshot is pinned by BYTES, and tools/lint_vendor_pin.py hashes
# the working tree. Line-ending translation would make that hash a property of
# the machine that checked out the repo: LF on the ubuntu CI runner, CRLF on a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true, from the identical commit. The lint
# would then be green in CI and red on the deploy machine, or the reverse,
# and the first thing anyone would suspect is drift that never happened.
#
# So: no conversion anywhere under vendor/. What upstream published is what we
# store and what we check out.
* -text
